course: dictionary
lesson: 16117
title: Whatsoever: at all
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Whatsoever is a word that makes a no stronger. When you say «There was no food whatsoever in the empty fridge», you mean there was none at all. Without whatsoever, the sentence would just say there was no food.
explain: Whatsoever usually comes after no, none or nothing. «She had nothing whatsoever to say about the plan» means she had nothing at all to say. Look for a clue: is there a no, none or nothing just before it? If so, whatsoever probably means at all.
explain: Whatsoever can also be an old, formal word that means whatever, or anything at all. «Take whatsoever you need from the shelf» means take anything you need. You will mostly meet this meaning in old stories or very formal writing.
fact: Whatsoever means at all.
fact: Whatsoever is used after no, none or nothing to make them stronger.
fact: «No idea whatsoever» means you have no idea at all.
fact: In old or formal writing, whatsoever can mean whatever or anything at all.
fact: Whatsoever is a formal word, so you will hear it more in serious speech and old books than in everyday chat.
exercise: «He had no fear whatsoever of the dark.» What does whatsoever mean here? | Somewhere else | Only sometimes | *At all | Very quickly
exercise: Which word does whatsoever usually come after to make it stronger? | Under | *No | Yesterday | Walk
exercise: «Take whatsoever you need from the shelf.» What does whatsoever mean? | A shelf for books | Nothing, not even one thing | Only the red things | *Anything at all
test: «She has no plans whatsoever for the holidays.» What does whatsoever tell you about the no? | *Not any plans at all | Plans for next year | Lots and lots of plans | Some plans, but only a few
test: Which sentence means there was no help at all? | Help came whatsoever quickly. | There was help, but it was far away. | *There was no help whatsoever. | There was help whatsoever, a little.
exam: Mia says «whatsoever» is just a fancy word for very. What is the best reply? | Yes, it means very, so Mia is right | It means happy, like a smile | *It means at all, and it comes after a no, so very does not fit | It means inside a box
